  "what": "- **Large GEMM problems**: Persistent kernels are most beneficial when the number of output tiles exceeds the SM count by at least 2-3x. - **Grouped GEMMs / MoE**: CLC can chain multiple problem instances, eliminating inter-kernel launch gaps. - **Workloads with uneven tile cost**: CLC's dynamic scheduling naturally handles variable-cost tiles (e.g., triangular attention masks).",
